## Troubleshooting

### Docker permission denied when starting Minikube

When running:

```bash
minikube start --driver=docker
/var/run/docker.sock

The error occurred because the current user session did not have active membership in the docker group.

Diagnosis

The following commands were used:

groups
getent group docker
ls -l /var/run/docker.sock

The user marcos was correctly listed in the docker group, and the Docker socket permissions were:

root docker

However, the current session had not yet loaded the new group membership.

Resolution: The virtual machine was restarted:
sudo reboot

After login, Docker was tested again without sudo:
docker ps

Then Minikube started successfully:

minikube start --driver=docker

Result

The Kubernetes cluster was successfully created and kubectl was configured to use the minikube cluster.

